From dad163ffb43cea45731d2fbe610733226c0e46d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:34:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-2-0099: skip ordered blocks and draw Darken spans

Extend the r25-2-0098 owned clipped-stroke executor with two measured,
ordered optimizations in one format-7 program.

Build conservative holder-space bounds for consecutive 256-command suffix
blocks from one bounds read in the existing parser pass. Replay rejects an
off-tile block by advancing its command and native side-stream counts without
changing painter order. Unknown bounds, stop-object rendering, or an
attached-object mutation epoch mismatch disable skipping and fail open to
ordered replay.

Admit exact opaque stroke-only Darken paths as owned native commands. AGG
rasterizes each object separately and sends its coverage plus the current
antialiased clip mask directly to PDFium's existing Darken scanline
compositor, removing the temporary BGRA object bitmap and second pixel pass.
Unsupported destination, group, printer, type-3, transparency, or live-state
cases fall back canonically at the same ordinal before destination mutation.

Keep the first 4096 commands canonical, retain the 96 MiB program cap, and add
compile/replay proof counters plus arithmetic and compiler representation
tests. No Kotlin/JNI scheduling or pixel-ownership policy changes.

